## 2026-07-24 (cont.) — book-library/LibriVox/AI-import removal complete

Follow-up to the remediation plan above. Removed the entire dead subsystem step 1
described: ~100 app files (Admin book/author/genre/series controllers, LibriVox
integration, Audible/GoogleBooks/Hardcover services, AI book-import tooling, book
filesystem/import jobs) plus ~200 test files exercising them, in commit c19b5ed4.
MySqlService.php: 2455 -> ~500 lines. DocumentStoreServiceInterface: 122 -> 42 methods
(the 42 kept are everything actually called by the 15 live-routed Api/ controllers +
the 6 kept Admin/ controllers (UserController, AccountRequestController, AdminController,
MessageController, MessagesController, BadgeController) + DocumentUserProvider +
CreateAdminUser command -- confirmed by grepping actual call sites, not guessing).

Kept but stubbed: getBook()/listBooks() now always return null/empty rather than
querying a `books` table that doesn't exist -- they used to hard-crash whenever
ApiHealthController or BookmarkApiController's live routes were hit.

Kept, not yet routed (per explicit instruction -- these need routes wired up, not
deletion): app/Http/Controllers/Admin/{UserController,AccountRequestController,
AdminController,MessageController,MessagesController,BadgeController}.php.

Explicitly NOT touched, needs its own decision: Skin/Theme controllers and gallery
views (SkinController, ThemeController, SkinAssetController, SkinWebController,
BuiltinSkinController, SkinService, ThemeService, resources/views/gallery/skins/*,
resources/views/admin/skins/*) -- also zero routes currently, same pattern as the
removed book stuff, but SKIN_CUSTOMIZATION_SPEC.md suggests this was meant to be a
real feature, not leftover cruft like LibriVox/books were. Ask before touching.

### Result

- `vendor/bin/phpstan analyse app --level=5`: 1000+ (fatal, couldn't complete) -> 197
  errors, all now in a genuinely different category (see below), not book-library
  leftovers.
- `php artisan test --testsuite=Unit,Feature`: went from **unable to boot at all**
  (referenced deleted classes) to 165 passing / 210 failing.
- Full `app + tests` PHPStan scan still needed as a final check once tests are settled.

### Remaining 197 app/ PHPStan errors -- a different, separate problem

These are NOT book-library leftovers. They're missing Eloquent model classes for
services that ARE kept/wanted, i.e. incomplete features, not stuff that "should never
have been brought to this repo":

- `App\Models\ReadingSession` -- used by UserReadingStatsService (kept, needed for
  getUserActivityData)
- `App\Models\Message` -- used by WorkflowMessagingService (kept, needed for
  getMessages/createMessage/acknowledgeMessage)
- `App\Models\Badge`, `App\Models\UserBadge` -- used by Admin/BadgeController (kept)
  and referenced from User model
- `App\Models\Playlist` -- used by ListeningGoalController (kept, live-routed!)
- `App\Models\UserBookStatus` -- referenced from User model
- Two now-genuinely-unused traits flagged by PHPStan itself: GenreMapping,
  IsolatesErrorHandlers (trivial to remove, just hadn't gotten to it)

Also: the `books` table still doesn't exist at all (no migration ever created it),
so any test fixture using `Book::factory()->create()` fails with "no such table:
books" -- this is the same architecture point from the entry above (book identity
should be string-based, not a real library table). This affects
BookmarkSyncControllerTest, StatisticsStreakTest, and probably others -- pre-existing,
confirmed present before any of today's book-library removal work, not a regression
from it.

### Remaining 210 failing tests

Re-run `php artisan test --testsuite=Unit,Feature` after picking up the model-class
work above and see what's left. Expect most of the current 210 to clear once
ReadingSession/Message/Badge/Playlist/UserBadge/UserBookStatus exist and the `books`
table question is resolved. Anything still failing after that is worth a fresh look --
don't assume it's more of the same.
